---
title: "withdrawExcessInvestedCapital (LegionPreLiquidApprovedSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_paused: investor withdraws excess capital
    q_check_paused --> q_check_ended: not paused
    q_check_paused --> q_revert_paused: contract paused
    q_check_ended --> q_check_not_claimed: hasEnded == true
    q_check_ended --> q_revert_not_ended: sale not ended
    q_check_not_claimed --> q_verify_sig: position.hasClaimedExcess == false
    q_check_not_claimed --> q_revert_claimed: already claimed
    q_verify_sig --> q_calc_excess: verify signature with reduced allocation terms
    q_verify_sig --> q_revert_sig: invalid signature
    q_calc_excess --> q_check_excess: excessAmount = position.investedCapital - acceptedAmount
    q_check_excess --> q_update: excessAmount > 0
    q_check_excess --> q_revert_no_excess: no excess
    q_update --> q_transfer: position.hasClaimedExcess = true
    q_transfer --> [*]: transfer(investor, excessAmount), emit ExcessCapitalWithdrawn(investor, excessAmount)
    q_revert_paused --> [*]: revert Paused
    q_revert_not_ended --> [*]: revert SaleNotEnded
    q_revert_claimed --> [*]: revert AlreadyClaimed
    q_revert_sig --> [*]: revert InvalidSignature
    q_revert_no_excess --> [*]: revert NoExcess

    note right of q_verify_sig
        INV-001: Uses signature verification (not Merkle proof) for excess claims
        INV-002: Reduced allocation signature authorizes lower amount than SAFT maximum
    end note
